### Visibility API walkthrough (VS Code REST Client)
### Run make dev and execute requests in order. No provider API keys are required.
### All answers are stub/sample data. Live collection will use Cloro.
### Explicit cookies keep users A and B separate.

@host = http://localhost:5173
@baseUrl = {{host}}/api/v1
@password = password123

### Signed out: 401
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{baseUrl}}/brands/11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111/runs

### Sign up A: 201
# @no-cookie-jar
# @name signupA
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"visibility-a-{{$guid}}@example.com","password":"{{password}}"}

### Create A's brand: 201
# @no-cookie-jar
# @name brandA
POST {{baseUrl}}/brands
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

{"name":"Northstar Metrics","domain":"northstar.example","country":"US"}

### Empty history: 200 with items: [] and standard page metadata
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{brandA.response.body.$.id}}/runs?page=1&pageSize=10
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### No prompts: 409 run_not_ready, prompts/empty
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{brandA.response.body.$.id}}/runs
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Add first manual prompt (already confirmed): 201
# @no-cookie-jar
# @name firstPrompt
POST {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{brandA.response.body.$.id}}/prompts
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

{"text":"Best analytics for startups?"}

### Add second prompt: 201
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{brandA.response.body.$.id}}/prompts
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

{"text":"Alternatives to Example Analytics?"}

### Start sample run with zero competitors: 202, total_results: 8
### Repeated POST while active returns the same run; after completion it creates another.
# @no-cookie-jar
# @name startRun
POST {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{brandA.response.body.$.id}}/runs
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Poll: 200, eventually succeeded and completed_results: 8 (including errors)
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{host}}{{startRun.response.body.$.status_url}}
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Inspect matrix: 200, 8 results, collector: stub, all four outcomes
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{host}}{{startRun.response.body.$.status_url}}/results?page=1&pageSize=40
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Delete a tracking prompt: 204. The saved matrix still contains its original text.
# @no-cookie-jar
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{brandA.response.body.$.id}}/prompts/{{firstPrompt.response.body.$.id}}
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Reload persisted history: 200, including original results after restarting the app
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{host}}{{startRun.response.body.$.status_url}}/results?page=1&pageSize=40
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Invalid pagination: 400 validation
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{host}}{{startRun.response.body.$.status_url}}/results?pageSize=101
Cookie: {{signupA.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Sign up B: 201
# @no-cookie-jar
# @name signupB
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"visibility-b-{{$guid}}@example.com","password":"{{password}}"}

### B cannot read A's run: 404
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{host}}{{startRun.response.body.$.status_url}}
Cookie: {{signupB.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### B cannot read A's answers: 404
# @no-cookie-jar
GET {{host}}{{startRun.response.body.$.status_url}}/results
Cookie: {{signupB.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### B cannot start A's run: 404
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{baseUrl}}/brands/{{brandA.response.body.$.id}}/runs
Cookie: {{signupB.response.headers.Set-Cookie}}

### Unconfirmed guard: use an existing draft from the optional drafting feature.
### Starting a run returns 409 run_not_ready until unconfirmed prompts/competitors
### are confirmed or removed. Automated integration tests seed drafts directly,
### including an unconfirmed row beyond page one, without provider calls.
